<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.Africa winding down oil stocks, now 4-1/2 months.</title>
<headline>S.Africa winding down oil stocks, now 4-1/2 months.</headline>
<dateline>CAPE TOWN 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The South African is gradually winding down its oil stocks to the three months supply levels recommended by the International Energy Agency, Deputy Minerals and Energy Affairs Minister Susan Shabangu said on Monday.</p>
<p>These stocks currently stand at about 55 million barrels, or about four-and-a-half months' supply.</p>
<p>Shabangu also said that South Africa was continually reviewing its sources of crude oil, which it has for years bought mainly from Iran. No tangible new supply agreements had been entered into but the government had an open policy, she added.</p>
<p>-- Lynda Loxton, Cape Town newsroom +27 21 25-2238</p>
</text>
